IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `oapa-nouns`
IMPORT `oapa-abortion-birth`

-- Offences against the Person Act 1861 -- TESTS for oapa-abortion-birth.l4 (sections 58
-- to 61).  Every expected value was decided from the section's text before the
-- assertion was written, and is stated beside it.

§ `Tests: abortion and concealing a birth`

§§ `Section 58`

-- unlawfully, the person is a woman who was with child, intended her own miscarriage,
-- administered to herself, used an instrument or other means upon herself, intended to
-- procure the miscarriage of a woman (with child or not), administered to or caused to be
-- taken by that woman, used an instrument or other means upon that woman
`s58 a woman with child administers to herself` MEANS `Conduct under section 58` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`s58 a woman with child uses an instrument upon herself` MEANS `Conduct under section 58` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`s58 another person administers to a woman` MEANS `Conduct under section 58` OF TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE
`s58 another person uses an instrument upon a woman who is not with child` MEANS `Conduct under section 58` OF TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE
`s58 a woman not with child administers to herself, under limb two as the words read` MEANS `Conduct under section 58` OF TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE
`s58 a woman who was not with child, limb one only` MEANS `Conduct under section 58` OF TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`s58 a woman with child acts on herself, not unlawfully` MEANS `Conduct under section 58` OF FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE
`s58 another person, not unlawfully` MEANS `Conduct under section 58` OF FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE
`s58 another person administers, no intent` MEANS `Conduct under section 58` OF TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE
`s58 intent, no act` MEANS `Conduct under section 58` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE

#ASSERT `s 58: administering drugs or using instruments to procure abortion` `s58 a woman with child administers to herself`
#ASSERT `s 58: limb one, a woman with child acting on herself` `s58 a woman with child administers to herself`
#ASSERT `s 58: administering drugs or using instruments to procure abortion` `s58 a woman with child uses an instrument upon herself`
#ASSERT `s 58: administering drugs or using instruments to procure abortion` `s58 another person administers to a woman`
#ASSERT `s 58: administering drugs or using instruments to procure abortion` `s58 another person uses an instrument upon a woman who is not with child`
-- limb one needs the woman to have been with child; limb two does not ("whether she be or
-- be not with child")
#ASSERT NOT (`s 58: limb one, a woman with child acting on herself` `s58 another person administers to a woman`)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 58: limb one, a woman with child acting on herself` `s58 a woman who was not with child, limb one only`)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 58: administering drugs or using instruments to procure abortion` `s58 a woman who was not with child, limb one only`)
-- limb two says "any woman": the words reach a woman acting on herself too
#ASSERT `s 58: limb two, any person acting upon a woman` `s58 a woman not with child administers to herself, under limb two as the words read`
#ASSERT NOT (`s 58: administering drugs or using instruments to procure abortion` `s58 a woman with child acts on herself, not unlawfully`)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 58: administering drugs or using instruments to procure abortion` `s58 another person, not unlawfully`)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 58: administering drugs or using instruments to procure abortion` `s58 another person administers, no intent`)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 58: administering drugs or using instruments to procure abortion` `s58 intent, no act`)
#ASSERT `s 58: what the text calls the offence` EQUALS felony
#ASSERT `s 58: the sentences the text states` EQUALS LIST `penal servitude` `for life`

§§ `Section 59`

-- unlawfully, supplied or procured a thing, knew it was intended to be unlawfully used
-- with intent to procure a miscarriage
`s59 supplied, knowing` MEANS `Conduct under section 59` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE
`s59 supplied, not knowing of the intended use` MEANS `Conduct under section 59` OF TRUE, TRUE, FALSE
`s59 knew, but did not supply or procure` MEANS `Conduct under section 59` OF TRUE, FALSE, TRUE
`s59 supplied, knowing, but not unlawfully` MEANS `Conduct under section 59` OF FALSE, TRUE, TRUE

#ASSERT `s 59: supplying drugs or instruments to procure abortion` `s59 supplied, knowing`
#ASSERT NOT (`s 59: supplying drugs or instruments to procure abortion` `s59 supplied, not knowing of the intended use`)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 59: supplying drugs or instruments to procure abortion` `s59 knew, but did not supply or procure`)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 59: supplying drugs or instruments to procure abortion` `s59 supplied, knowing, but not unlawfully`)
#ASSERT `s 59: what the text calls the offence` EQUALS misdemeanor
#ASSERT `s 59: the sentences the text states` EQUALS LIST `penal servitude` `for a term the text does not state`

§§ `Section 60`

-- a woman was delivered of a child, secret disposition of the dead body, endeavoured to
-- conceal the birth, the person is the woman delivered
`s60 the mother` MEANS `Conduct under section 60` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE
`s60 another person` MEANS `Conduct under section 60` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE
`s60 disposed of the body but not to conceal the birth` MEANS `Conduct under section 60` OF TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE
`s60 endeavoured to conceal but no secret disposition` MEANS `Conduct under section 60` OF TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE
`s60 no woman was delivered of a child` MEANS `Conduct under section 60` OF FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE

#ASSERT `s 60: concealing the birth of a child` `s60 the mother`
-- "every person": the woman or anyone else
#ASSERT `s 60: concealing the birth of a child` `s60 another person`
#ASSERT NOT (`s 60: concealing the birth of a child` `s60 disposed of the body but not to conceal the birth`)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 60: concealing the birth of a child` `s60 endeavoured to conceal but no secret disposition`)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 60: concealing the birth of a child` `s60 no woman was delivered of a child`)
#ASSERT `s 60: what the text calls the offence` EQUALS misdemeanor
#ASSERT `s 60: the sentences the text states` EQUALS LIST `imprisonment` (`for a term not exceeding` 24)

§§ `Section 61`

#ASSERT `s 61: blank in this text` EQUALS "Section 61 shows only its number and a row of dots; there is nothing to encode."
